1
00:00:01,836 --> 00:00:12,118
The ops queue: active, at-risk and breached counts come straight from the SLA engine.

2
00:00:16,524 --> 00:00:26,806
Filters run server-side; each row shows its governing rule and a live countdown.

3
00:00:39,336 --> 00:00:53,986
The case workspace: booking context, classified intent, case brief and main thread.

4
00:00:55,032 --> 00:01:09,682
Side conversations keep their own explicit recipients, independent of the main thread.

5
00:01:14,390 --> 00:01:28,840
A transfer moves queue and owner only, then verifies the recipients are unchanged.

6
00:01:30,672 --> 00:01:39,811
Routing: hard filters first, then the 35 / 25 / 25 / 15 score with every term visible.

7
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:52,867
Run the assignment and the decision is written to the immutable routing audit.

8
00:02:02,708 --> 00:02:08,465
The escalation war room: real ownership handover, holiday-adjusted deadlines.

9
00:02:12,988 --> 00:02:18,745
Countdowns tick against the stored effective due date, not a static flag.

10
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:30,952
Product intelligence: intents, suppliers, refund bottlenecks and regional performance.

11
00:02:31,744 --> 00:02:39,136
Recurring supplier plus intent patterns become bug proposals with evidence.

12
00:02:37,552 --> 00:02:44,944
A 50,000-row export streams from a server iterator and is validated from disk.

13
00:02:50,580 --> 00:03:01,444
The simulation lab runs the five seeded journeys against the live API.

14
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:16,964
Every step shows the actual response next to the expectation.
